1
00:00:00,142 --> 00:00:02,881
I'll show you. I'll read, and you can write it down.

2
00:00:02,882 --> 00:00:05,481
Okay, let's do it that way.

3
00:00:05,482 --> 00:00:07,441
Well, maybe I'll add something, just a bit.

4
00:00:07,442 --> 00:00:08,401
Great.

5
00:00:08,402 --> 00:00:09,356
What's this?

6
00:00:09,357 --> 00:00:12,631
It was only on one side there.

7
00:00:12,632 --> 00:00:15,001
And this is on the other side.

8
00:00:15,002 --> 00:00:22,181
I've had this birthmark since birth, and here's a pimple, grandma.

9
00:00:22,182 --> 00:00:24,161
I can't see you. Far right.

10
00:00:24,162 --> 00:00:26,411
Is that you? Yes, I see now.

11
00:00:26,412 --> 00:00:28,151
There I am standing.

12
00:00:28,152 --> 00:00:29,246
Yes, I see.

13
00:00:29,247 --> 00:00:33,691
And this is my aunt Marusya, grandmother Dusya's sister.

14
00:00:33,692 --> 00:00:34,511
I see.

15
00:00:34,512 --> 00:00:39,731
Here's grandmother Dusya, still young, before the war.

16
00:00:39,732 --> 00:00:44,641
And here's your father, this is us in Moscow.

17
00:00:46,522 --> 00:00:47,621
My great-grandfather.

18
00:00:47,622 --> 00:00:51,031
So this is your father? Where?

19
00:00:52,722 --> 00:00:53,731
Well, who else?

20
00:00:54,117 --> 00:01:00,731
A girl named Stalina, who was shot along with her grandmother and great-grandmother.

21
00:01:00,732 --> 00:01:01,781
Show me.

22
00:01:01,782 --> 00:01:03,851
So young. Yes.

23
00:01:03,852 --> 00:01:08,351
Well, this was before the war. Yes.

24
00:01:08,352 --> 00:01:14,911
And in that one, in forty-first, she was six years old.

25
00:01:14,912 --> 00:01:20,101
So they shot a small child too. Hello there.

26
00:01:20,102 --> 00:01:27,531
When the war began, we lived in the village of Nechayannoe, beyond Nikolaev toward Odessa.

27
00:01:27,532 --> 00:01:30,226
About thirty kilometers, I don't remember exactly.

28
00:01:30,227 --> 00:01:36,025
German air raids were quite intensive,

29
00:01:36,026 --> 00:01:39,891
and we had to flee from there.

30
00:01:39,892 --> 00:01:41,316
Who else was there? So you...

31
00:01:41,317 --> 00:01:48,691
Well, grandmother and grandfather. Grandmother Manya and grandfather Fedor, my mother, my brother and I.

32
00:01:48,692 --> 00:01:50,631
And there was also aunt Shura.

33
00:01:50,632 --> 00:01:59,261
I remember a long basement with a vaulted ceiling.

34
00:01:59,262 --> 00:02:00,321
Yes.

35
00:02:00,322 --> 00:02:06,921
People were sitting along the walls there.

36
00:02:06,922 --> 00:02:14,071
What I remember, before my eyes: a huge pile of books in the courtyard.

37
00:02:14,072 --> 00:02:19,511
There was a library there, a teacher training school.

38
00:02:19,512 --> 00:02:25,041
I don't know if our side threw them out during liberation, or if the Germans did.

39
00:02:25,042 --> 00:02:32,541
That huge pile of books is what I remember most.

40
00:02:48,802 --> 00:02:51,471
Europe in struggle.

41
00:02:51,472 --> 00:02:56,862
The fight for a continent that is whole and peaceful,

42
00:02:56,863 --> 00:03:00,231
for a free and independent Europe.

43
00:03:00,232 --> 00:03:05,081
The fight for our values and our democracies.

44
00:03:05,082 --> 00:03:13,200
The fight for our freedom and ability to determine our own destiny.

45
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:18,941
Make no mistake. This is a fight for our future.

46
00:03:18,942 --> 00:03:21,630
In the end, we Europeans

47
00:03:21,631 --> 00:03:26,471
are not used to feeling comfortable speaking in such terms.

48
00:03:26,472 --> 00:03:30,711
Because our union is fundamentally a peace project.

49
00:03:30,712 --> 00:03:34,291
So yes, Europe must fight.

50
00:03:34,292 --> 00:03:40,106
Volodymyr Zelenskyy entered the US Congress chamber to a standing ovation on Wednesday.

51
00:03:40,107 --> 00:03:45,733
The Ukrainian president was there to address a joint session of the Senate and House of Representatives,

52
00:03:45,734 --> 00:03:50,061
hoping to convince them to continue funding his country's defense against Russia.

53
00:03:50,062 --> 00:03:54,471
No one has contributed as much as Europe.

54
00:03:54,472 --> 00:03:59,201
About 170 billion euros in military and financial aid to date,

55
00:03:59,202 --> 00:04:00,921
and more will be needed.

56
00:04:00,922 --> 00:04:04,427
I really want to show you this powerful moment. Listen.

57
00:04:08,542 --> 00:04:14,085
It was a powerful moment when a standing ovation occurred

58
00:04:14,086 --> 00:04:17,550
for Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy.

59
00:04:17,551 --> 00:04:23,221
Today the situation in the East is stabilized. As much as possible.

60
00:04:23,222 --> 00:04:29,581
Especially at a moment when Russia wants to launch counter-offensive actions.

61
00:04:29,582 --> 00:04:34,507
That is, not just quantity, but to defend,

62
00:04:34,508 --> 00:04:38,201
to stabilize, to hold the situation, you need parity.

63
00:04:38,202 --> 00:04:42,301
And to attack, you need greater force.

64
00:04:42,302 --> 00:04:46,868
There is a real war in Ukraine against the entire world,

65
00:04:46,869 --> 00:04:49,151
against democracy and values.

66
00:04:49,152 --> 00:04:54,001
I don't want to repeat these words, maybe they're tiresome to some,

67
00:04:54,002 --> 00:04:59,336
but they're only tiresome to those who aren't fighting and don't know

68
00:04:59,337 --> 00:05:02,098
what war is, and haven't lost children.

69
00:05:02,917 --> 00:05:09,971
And so we can't talk like that. We now have this kind of war.

70
00:05:09,972 --> 00:05:13,531
There is no war. But it can come.

71
00:05:13,532 --> 00:05:16,531
To Europe and to the United States.

72
00:05:16,532 --> 00:05:21,326
Because, thank God, missiles don't reach the United States.

73
00:05:21,327 --> 00:05:28,576
But we have with you not dialogue, but a situation with Putin.

74
00:05:29,866 --> 00:05:33,657
And tomorrow missiles could reach any country.

75
00:05:36,142 --> 00:05:42,473
And therefore, if to Europe, and missiles are already flying there,

76
00:05:42,474 --> 00:05:48,101
if Putin, Russia, his army comes to Europe...

77
00:05:48,102 --> 00:05:50,061
My name is Dmytruk Artem.

78
00:05:50,062 --> 00:05:52,034
I am an Orthodox Christian,

79
00:05:52,035 --> 00:05:54,006
a patriot of my country,

80
00:05:54,007 --> 00:05:57,951
currently a member of the Ukrainian parliament.

81
00:06:05,251 --> 00:06:08,146
This story is not about me.

82
00:06:08,148 --> 00:06:12,701
This is a story about the Ukraine that Zelenskyy created,

83
00:06:12,701 --> 00:06:17,908
and about the repressions that tens of thousands

84
00:06:17,909 --> 00:06:21,627
of people in Ukraine have experienced and continue to experience.

85
00:06:21,628 --> 00:06:24,957
In our country, a criminal organization

86
00:06:24,958 --> 00:06:27,176
like the TCC is gaining momentum.

87
00:06:27,178 --> 00:06:30,346
They're loading the guy up, by force!

88
00:06:30,718 --> 00:06:33,379
Look, faces, faces!

89
00:06:34,164 --> 00:06:40,146
Today, citizens of Ukraine are afraid to live in their own country.

90
00:06:40,148 --> 00:06:42,976
Guys, why are you holding him by force?

91
00:06:44,002 --> 00:06:46,447
Get away from me! Son of a...!

92
00:06:46,838 --> 00:06:52,711
TCC workers not only grab people all over the country,

93
00:06:52,712 --> 00:06:55,321
they steal, beat people with impunity.

94
00:06:55,322 --> 00:06:58,164
They're kidnapping a person.

95
00:07:04,117 --> 00:07:07,047
Look, people are filming this, it's TCC.

96
00:07:07,048 --> 00:07:08,854
A completely innocent person

97
00:07:08,855 --> 00:07:12,466
who was just walking down the street, they're grabbing.

98
00:07:12,468 --> 00:07:15,447
[inaudible]

99
00:07:17,044 --> 00:07:18,490
We're talking today about the fact

100
00:07:18,490 --> 00:07:23,029
that in Ukraine from February to November 2022, there existed

101
00:07:23,030 --> 00:07:24,164
an SBU concentration camp.

102
00:07:34,138 --> 00:07:36,140
And it specialized in

103
00:07:36,141 --> 00:07:38,644
bringing various kinds of people there

104
00:07:38,645 --> 00:07:40,146
through extrajudicial means.

105
00:07:40,148 --> 00:07:43,297
That is, they were simply grabbed on the street.

106
00:07:45,597 --> 00:07:47,437
[inaudible]

107
00:07:49,398 --> 00:07:53,682
Help! Help!

108
00:07:54,523 --> 00:07:57,454
And he sits in the basement at TCC.

109
00:07:57,455 --> 00:08:01,151
They impose narratives on him there, psychologically pressure him.

110
00:08:07,737 --> 00:08:10,021
He has no access to a lawyer,

111
00:08:10,021 --> 00:08:13,833
no relatives, no food, no water, nothing.

112
00:08:14,938 --> 00:08:17,458
Wait, you... damn it!

113
00:08:17,458 --> 00:08:19,078
Let's talk!

114
00:08:19,606 --> 00:08:21,656
I don't want to fight!

115
00:08:21,998 --> 00:08:24,210
Of course, many people break.

116
00:08:24,211 --> 00:08:26,976
Of course, many agree to something.

117
00:08:32,538 --> 00:08:37,856
Move it! Hey!

118
00:08:40,337 --> 00:08:42,057
Listen, I'm a person

119
00:08:42,058 --> 00:08:43,662
who was subjected to torture,

120
00:08:43,663 --> 00:08:48,477
and I'll tell you for certain that it's impossible to endure torture.

121
00:08:49,212 --> 00:08:52,380
They sprayed me with a gas canister!

122
00:08:52,380 --> 00:08:54,455
People! Sprayed with a canister!

123
00:08:55,389 --> 00:08:55,990
People!

124
00:08:56,278 --> 00:08:58,251
People! They sprayed with a canister!

125
00:09:00,118 --> 00:09:03,672
When you're tortured, you'll say,

126
00:09:03,673 --> 00:09:07,120
sign, agree to anything.

127
00:09:07,121 --> 00:09:12,046
Especially when they manipulate with your relatives or loved ones.

128
00:09:12,048 --> 00:09:16,092
You know yourself what will happen.

129
00:09:16,093 --> 00:09:22,107
Everything will be fine. They say "No." No one gets punished.

130
00:09:22,108 --> 00:09:23,296
They say "no."

131
00:09:23,940 --> 00:09:28,646
Because, unfortunately, no one can protect them.

132
00:09:28,647 --> 00:09:31,904
Why don't you make it so people go normally to the armed forces?

133
00:09:31,905 --> 00:09:33,207
What kind of racketeering is this?

134
00:09:33,208 --> 00:09:34,659
What year is this?

135
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:37,562
Beating people, climbing into cars.

136
00:09:38,036 --> 00:09:41,344
I have in my hands witness testimonies

137
00:09:41,345 --> 00:09:44,230
from those who went through this concentration camp,

138
00:09:44,231 --> 00:09:47,647
who were there for six months.

139
00:09:47,648 --> 00:09:50,434
They were constantly kept with bags on their heads,

140
00:09:50,435 --> 00:09:52,757
lying on the floor in a gym.

141
00:09:52,758 --> 00:09:56,125
They were beaten, subjected to bodily harm.

142
00:10:00,509 --> 00:10:01,544
But this is a human being!

143
00:10:01,695 --> 00:10:02,487
What are you doing?

144
00:10:03,858 --> 00:10:05,607
This video is from Krasnograd.

145
00:10:07,818 --> 00:10:09,797
Kharkiv region.

146
00:10:09,798 --> 00:10:13,857
Confessional, so-called, testimonies against whoever they say,

147
00:10:13,858 --> 00:10:15,490
whoever they point their finger at.

148
00:10:16,178 --> 00:10:19,265
Don't beat him! Why are you beating him?!

149
00:10:25,047 --> 00:10:27,350
All our citizens want to live in

150
00:10:27,351 --> 00:10:29,682
a democratic free country.

151
00:10:29,683 --> 00:10:34,566
All our citizens want to read and speak in their native language,

152
00:10:34,567 --> 00:10:37,672
whether it's Ukrainian or Russian.

153
00:10:38,503 --> 00:10:42,887
They want to honor their heroes in different regions.

154
00:10:42,888 --> 00:10:48,226
They want to go to the church they choose, not one imposed on them.

155
00:10:48,228 --> 00:10:49,843
I'm ethnically Ukrainian.

156
00:10:49,844 --> 00:10:55,763
I speak the language that is mainly used here in the Donetsk region.

157
00:10:56,308 --> 00:10:58,157
What are you doing?! Help!

158
00:10:59,130 --> 00:11:00,338
Why are you touching him?

159
00:11:00,931 --> 00:11:02,196
They threw out the bag!

160
00:11:02,872 --> 00:11:04,991
Help!

161
00:11:05,358 --> 00:11:06,447
I understand you perfectly.

162
00:11:06,448 --> 00:11:08,347
Why don't you understand me?

163
00:11:08,348 --> 00:11:10,621
Did you come here to protect me?

164
00:11:10,623 --> 00:11:14,435
Or did you come to humiliate me just because I was born here?

165
00:11:14,436 --> 00:11:15,822
Because I'm Ukrainian!

166
00:11:15,822 --> 00:11:17,963
You want to humiliate me for that?

167
00:11:18,625 --> 00:11:19,910
Let go, damn it!

168
00:11:22,180 --> 00:11:23,766
Let him go!

169
00:11:23,767 --> 00:11:27,092
Let go of his legs. Let go.

170
00:11:27,093 --> 00:11:28,620
Thank you.

171
00:11:29,325 --> 00:11:31,208
Come on, let's go!

172
00:11:31,728 --> 00:11:35,856
I don't want to communicate with such a person who humiliates their own people.

173
00:11:35,858 --> 00:11:38,642
Doesn't protect them, but humiliates them. I'm happy for you.

174
00:11:38,643 --> 00:11:40,507
That you're such a person.

175
00:11:40,508 --> 00:11:43,436
Our faith cannot be forbidden.

176
00:11:43,438 --> 00:11:48,621
Faith is eternal, faith is glorious, our faith is Orthodox.

177
00:12:03,438 --> 00:12:08,353
My citizens, the citizens of Ukraine, who are defending, paying the highest price.

178
00:12:08,354 --> 00:12:10,364
They're defending freedom.

179
00:12:10,644 --> 00:12:15,503
I'm very glad to feel this sentiment, that this is the price

180
00:12:15,504 --> 00:12:16,911
that they must pay.

181
00:12:16,913 --> 00:12:25,711
We are giving our best people, the strongest, the most valuable.

182
00:12:26,159 --> 00:12:29,073
And we had to flee from there.

183
00:12:29,074 --> 00:12:33,063
I mean, this is a high price,

184
00:12:33,064 --> 00:12:35,252
a very high price, thousands of people who are killed.

185
00:12:35,252 --> 00:12:39,714
Who's beating him? They're strangling him! They're beating him!

186
00:12:39,714 --> 00:12:44,923
The Zelenskyy regime tried to kill me several times for my position.

187
00:12:44,924 --> 00:12:51,603
Life will defeat death, and light will defeat darkness.

188
00:12:51,604 --> 00:12:55,313
Glory to Ukraine!

189
00:13:01,494 --> 00:13:09,673
We are giving our lives for values, for rights, for freedom, for the desire to be equal just like you.

190
00:13:09,674 --> 00:13:15,213
This is our task of honor, dear friends, brothers and sisters.

191
00:13:15,214 --> 00:13:18,763
Ban Telegram in Ukraine right now.

192
00:13:18,764 --> 00:13:24,413
I remember before my eyes a huge pile of books in the courtyard.

193
00:13:24,414 --> 00:13:25,753
Help.

194
00:13:27,548 --> 00:13:28,753
Guys, they're strangling!

195
00:13:29,401 --> 00:13:31,673
Help, please!

196
00:13:31,674 --> 00:13:43,603
I want the whole world to know: fascists took my husband and drove him away, there's no contact with him.

197
00:13:43,604 --> 00:13:47,818
This is after I buried my children.

198
00:13:48,068 --> 00:13:49,405
Who are you?

199
00:14:02,474 --> 00:14:06,585
So they shot a small child too. Hello there.

200
00:14:10,677 --> 00:14:11,918
She was about six years old.

201
00:14:13,390 --> 00:14:14,663
Let go!

202
00:14:15,651 --> 00:14:19,533
Why are you taking the man away? What are you doing?

203
00:14:19,534 --> 00:14:22,633
What are you doing? What are you doing?

204
00:14:22,634 --> 00:14:24,833
Hey, show your face!

205
00:14:24,834 --> 00:14:27,753
Let the person go!

206
00:14:27,754 --> 00:14:29,793
Let the person go!

207
00:14:31,788 --> 00:14:32,853
What are you doing?

208
00:14:32,914 --> 00:14:40,433
Let the person go! Let go!
